      "body": "Register MLAAttention with the compressed-tensors KV-cache quantization method and map Kimi-K2.5/K2.6 checkpoint q/k/v scales into the model's nested MLA attention module.\r\n\r\nKeep the generic cache-scale mapper unchanged; all scale-name translation is scoped to Kimi.\r\n\r\nFixes intel/auto-round#2370.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n## Overview\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n## Claims\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n## Validation\r\n\r\nValidated on vLLM 0.32.0 using 4x B200 GPUs (`tensor_parallel_size=4`) with [`intel-ai/Kimi-K2.6-MXFP4-FP8ATTN-CT-AutoRound`](https://huggingface.co/intel-ai/Kimi-K2.6-MXFP4-FP8ATTN-CT-AutoRound) (106 shards, 524.76 GiB).\r\n\r\n- All 106/106 shards loaded with zero `*_scale is not loaded` warnings.\r\n- All 183 checkpoint q/k/v scales (61 layers x q/k/v) exactly matched the post-load scale buffers on every TP rank:\r\n\r\n```text\r\nCHECKPOINT_SCALES=183\r\nRANK=0 LOADED=183 MISSING=0 EXTRA=0 MISMATCH=0\r\nRANK=1 LOADED=183 MISSING=0 EXTRA=0 MISMATCH=0\r\nRANK=2 LOADED=183 MISSING=0 EXTRA=0 MISMATCH=0\r\nRANK=3 LOADED=183 MISSING=0 EXTRA=0 MISMATCH=0\r\nSCALE_VERIFICATION_PASS 183/183 exact matches on every rank\r\n```\r\n\r\n- [`examples/basic/offline_inference/generate.py`](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/blob/main/examples/basic/offline_inference/generate.py) exited with status 0 and generated coherent text for all four prompts:\r\n\r\nhttps://huggingface.co/intel-ai/Kimi-K2.6-MXFP4-FP8ATTN-CT-AutoRound\r\n\r\n```text\r\nPrompt: 'Hello, my name is'\r\nGenerated text: ' David and I am a professional photographer...'\r\n\r\nPrompt: 'The president of the United States is'\r\nGenerated text: ' the head of state and head of government of the United States...'\r\n\r\nPrompt: 'The capital of France is'\r\nGenerated text: ' Paris. The capital of the United States is Washington, D.C....'\r\n\r\nPrompt: 'The future of AI is'\r\nGenerated text: \" here, and it's not just about robots taking over the world...\"\r\n```\r\n\r\nGeneration command:\r\n\r\n```bash\r\npython examples/basic/offline_inference/generate.py \\\r\n  --model intel-ai/Kimi-K2.6-MXFP4-FP8ATTN-CT-AutoRound \\\r\n  --trust-remote-code \\\r\n  --tensor-parallel-size 4 \\\r\n  --max-model-len 4096 \\\r\n  --max-num-seqs 1 \\\r\n  --gpu-memory-utilization 0.90 \\\r\n  --enforce-eager \\\r\n  --max-tokens 64 \\\r\n  --temperature 0\r\n```\r\n\r\n## Details\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n<details>\r\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\r\n\r\n- [ ] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\r\n- [ ] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\r\n\r\n- [ ] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\r\n- [ ] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\r\n- [ ] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\r\n- [ ] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\r\n</details>\r\n\r\n",
      "changedFiles": 2,
